# Pins for the Python<->C parity harness inputs (test/pyc_parity/pyc_parity.py).
# wav:<path>  sha256 of a tracked source wav (path relative to the aec root).
# f32:<input>_<mic|ref>  sha256 of the float32 array the generator produces
#   (rec8/rec48 = scipy resample_poly of the 16 kHz recording; echo/speechdt/dtb = seeded scenes.py;
#   <clip stem> = mic/far-end of a blind-set clip, truncated to the shorter channel).
# A mismatch means the audio changed (numpy/scipy drift or an edit): the baseline moved, so the run refuses.
# Regenerate (maintainers only): pyc_parity_aec.sh --write-pins
